.TH OCAML-MUTANTS 1 "2026-08-29" "ocaml-mutants 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ocaml-mutants \- type-aware mutation testing for Dune projects
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ocaml-mutants
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Discovers typed OCaml mutations in an isolated workspace snapshot, supervises
tests, and stores versioned evidence locally. With no arguments an interactive
TTY opens the full-screen UI; a non-TTY invocation exits 2.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
Measure mutations. Complete measurement exits 0 regardless of survivors.
.TP
.B check [RUN_ID]
Apply configured policy: pass 0, violation 1, unusable evidence 2.
.TP
.B report [RUN_ID]
Render terminal, JSON, HTML, Markdown, SARIF, or Stryker output.
.TP
.B plan, merge
Create and combine deterministic CI shards.
.TP
.B list, ui, doctor
Discover mutants, browse evidence, or diagnose the environment.
.TP
.B config init|show|check|migrate
Manage `.ocaml-mutants.toml` version 2.
.TP
.B cache stats|gc|clean
Inspect and maintain the capability-protected local store.
.TP
.B mutant show|rerun|apply|revert|expect
Resolve actionable mutants with guarded source/config edits.
.SH TERMINAL UI
The live UI shows each settled mutant's diff, executed tests, bounded output,
evidence, coverage, and expectation state before the final report is published.
Use
.B ui --color=auto|always|never
or
.B ui --no-color
to control styling. The
.B NO_COLOR
environment variable selects the full-screen monochrome mode unless
.B --color=always
is explicit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Run uses 0 for complete measurement, 2 for usage/infrastructure/incomplete
evidence, and 130 for interruption. Check additionally uses 1 for policy
violations on valid evidence.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .ocaml-mutants.toml
Optional version 2 workspace configuration.
.TP
.I .ocaml-mutants/undo
Owner-private undo records created by explicit mutant apply.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation at https://github.com/P4suta/ocaml-mutants
